<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How do the US midterms work, and why are they so important for Trump's presidency?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbbd5a97c13ba3eb44728408f02dafaf9740bd2135d565b83f6747e7a6104ef</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-do-the-us-midterms-work-and-why-are-they-so-important-for-trump-s-presidency/a-79789932--5c980e8318e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-do-the-us-midterms-work-and-why-are-they-so-important-for-trump-s-presidency/a-79789932?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US voters are electing a new Congress. The results will be decisive for the future of the United States, and a judgment on Donald Trump's second term as president.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Evacuation from Oleshky: How are preparations going?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:822c630e409505eb879f43657a09963bb15b6157719ed1662876d659fe85ca73</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001--e77f75613f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A lawyer with the Save Ukraine Foundation, Myroslava Kharchenko, told DW about what has been happening in Russian-occupied Oleshky since a temporary ceasefire brokered by Melania Trump took effect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>One year on, families seek justice after election violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf6f4d1e00314265cbc9cd6591eb1759cc10fa9849847257887271a5731b2f8e</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105--19ee0afa750b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One year after Tanzania's deadly post-election violence, families are still seeking answers. A government inquiry recorded 518 deaths. DW research has documented apparent use of excessive force by security forces.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What would a new Israeli government mean for Arab neighbors? More of the same is expected, with some small positives predicted.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3258327230a74a277e1937559972b4be76c400829afce823c3bd6915c9270e3f</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-a-new-israeli-government-mean-for-arab-neighbors-more-of-the-same-is-expected-with-some-s/a-79788174--4047f4a42d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-a-new-israeli-government-mean-for-arab-neighbors-more-of-the-same-is-expected-with-some-small-positives-predicted/a-79788174?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Israeli government is unlikely to bring big changes on controversial topics like Palestinian statehood and Israeli troops in Lebanon and Syria, experts say. Some small positives may be possible though.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's Zelenskyy irked by US-Russia-China summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cc5a57e8430d59bf532d5886b8b3fbda923f003749a027ae1f7a8a2e09dd025</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-zelenskyy-irked-by-us-russia-china-summit/a-79788616--52eeb4f3288e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-zelenskyy-irked-by-us-russia-china-summit/a-79788616?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volodymyr Zelenskyy has voiced his concerns about a probable meeting between the leaders of the US, China and Russia next month. Plus, a localized truce appeared to be holding in the town of Oleshky.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro lands in US, declares himself 'president-elect' of Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bd1348dee84865d5a80693b41a7539dec3048039106a9d3a5035a04469c4491</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-president-elect-of-brazil/a-79788659--f31b0bd8941e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-president-elect-of-brazil/a-79788659?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family landed in Florida early on Wednesday. Facing money laundering allegations, he fled just days after refusing to concede defeat to incumbent Lula.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish train crash leaves 68 dead, PM Sanchez declares 3 days of mourning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fec49b87a51854623e9b46316a41c5b165624ad95c1a4cec64641c211a40ad93</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-train-crash-leaves-68-dead-pm-sanchez-declares-3-days-of-mourning/live-79785087--27257c567f3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-train-crash-leaves-68-dead-pm-sanchez-declares-3-days-of-mourning/live-79785087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two high-speed trains carrying hundreds of passengers collided south of Madrid. Spain's transport minister said one of the trains was told to continue its journey despite a "red signal" being in effect. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5ed55643657f7a62530839ab7bca82dbf29ca635b456b4387ac653388ed2f6c</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests in Germany: Is France-style violence looming?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e255b48bdebdbfbe4c12041de106c69670b7c865af399b1c98efd1a493a4946c</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050--fb575275c7ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Young people in Germany will take to the streets this weekend to demand education and action on climate change. Politicians warn that the protests could become violent, as in France, but the situations are different.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Israel election: Netanyahu-led bloc in slight lead with more than 80% of votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0e8ce2321cbbe273b88f281b9a797d436a8c110b86ec92f171d4e9552556d6d</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-election-netanyahu-led-bloc-in-slight-lead-with-more-than-80-of-votes-counted/live-79713839--ce4e0610679a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-election-netanyahu-led-bloc-in-slight-lead-with-more-than-80-of-votes-counted/live-79713839?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While partial results show the pro-Netanyahu bloc ahead of the anti-Netanyahu bloc, the final tally could take days. Neither grouping is expected to win a majority, with tough coalition talks ahead. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17104b5db60cd74f0ca5c2ae5d662194806b61a97fc03da23e42158928d66903</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62d1717c1d1b335610ae582be343625451931a678505369639966a28ddcb0dec</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parties debate who should succeed President Steinmeier, with several women under discussion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57def128fa39cdb362bf957ad01f086030837101d589e295c54dc91f8706f8f8</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discuss/live-79783779--1c6d43c0de10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discussion/live-79783779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's political parties are weighing possible successors to President Frank-Walter Steinmeier, with no candidate agreed yet. Meanwhile, a poll suggests most Germans are giving Halloween a miss this year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2665e7cc52fe84e49bfdf51994cb6cff959018671c14465699b0d3d90389ddb9</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens of people killed after high-speed trains collide in central Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f9ed0de36448011a5bddabe24b9c79572cd904b53f15b95358c411143804827</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-of-people-killed-after-high-speed-trains-collide-in-central-spain/a-79784119--b7f767ed615f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-of-people-killed-after-high-speed-trains-collide-in-central-spain/a-79784119?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 68 people have been killed in a train crash in central Spain, local authorities have confirmed. Rail services between Madrid and Seville have been suspended.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:114e420152a4db880f959ff8c5437a5162935a307739406e027beb1ccc0e305b</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian police shoot dead assailant at Israeli Embassy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c835d9ae1d507688deddc63bd53aaf0c3d59f77879ca4d938b2bc1f80881a5c4</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905--d152a4aa69fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A "minor" has been killed by police after attacking a guard at Israel's embassy in Belgrade with knives, the interior minister says. Ivica Dacic said police had declared the highest terror alert after the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cyclone Arnab turns deadly after landfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8fceb225deb4e2691b33d709800f0716f16f5c3183dbc4dd37aa8ea5f2243af</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T04:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323--51b97fb16b83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Arnab killed at least three people in Andhra Pradesh after making landfall earlier today. Also, a new report says India is paying a steep economic cost over heat. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Experts urge 'global health emergency' as climate harms accelerate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8442add2fbe2cbe0e1ddd2cee6d92083ef777cb6bd2892104a609145be59f4e0</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T00:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/experts-urge-global-health-emergency-as-climate-harms-accelerate/a-79773232--6973c15b8839.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/experts-urge-global-health-emergency-as-climate-harms-accelerate/a-79773232?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Lancet report reveals the growing toll of climate change on human health, from rising heat deaths and drought to food insecurity and lost livelihoods.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt orders closure of independent news site Mada Masr</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fb30d326ff27fb03383b41a628d75e4f3bdedf17026557843bd50b90983a95e</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842--499fd97538eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Editor-in-chief Lina Attalah was briefly detained and fined over licensing violations. Rights groups condemned the ruling as a major blow to press freedom in Egypt, where independent media face growing pressure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US amid investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f842eb3fe9c8b95fa37dccdb1ede21491984619ec285cb37e96ac495083346f5</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:11:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T22:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-amid-investigation/a-79781094--17bcb76430fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-amid-investigation/a-79781094?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro, who lost to incumbent Lula in Sunday's presidential election, has reportedly fled the country. Bolsonaro, who is facing multiple corruption probes, has refused to concede.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
